# Containers' UI, reusing Chromium's (src/chrome/browser/containers/android, docs/containers.md):
# - ChromeContextMenuPopulator.java: a link's Open in container, a chooser of the containers;
#   no Preview page in a container, as the preview would load outside it.
# - TabGridViewBinder.java: a tab switcher row has a line in its container's color.
# - TabStripSceneLayer.java: so has a tab on the tablet tab strip, in Chromium's tab underline.
# - main_preferences.xml: Settings → Containers, after Privacy and security.
# - TabSwitcherActionMenuCoordinator.java, ToolbarManager.java: New tab in container, after New tab
#   in the tab switcher button's long-press menu; the button's dot in the current tab's container color.
# - TabGridContextMenuCoordinator.java: Reopen in container, in a tab's menu in the tab switcher.
# - HubToolbarCoordinator.java, TabSwitcherPane.java: a long press on the tab switcher's New tab
#   button opens a new tab in a container.
